  <section class="game-howto" aria-label="How to play">
    <h2>How to play — Punctuation Storm</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Fragments fall in four lanes. Every one is punctuation-heavy on purpose — <code>("wait,")</code>, <code>[see p. 12];</code>, <code>"Don't!"</code>, <code>x = {a: 1};</code> — because punctuation is where most typists are slowest.</li>
      <li><strong>No commit key.</strong> The moment what you have typed matches a fragment on screen exactly, that fragment clears and the field empties. Several fragments contain spaces, so space cannot be the submit key the way it is in Boss Battle.</li>
      <li><strong>Scoring:</strong> 10 points per punctuation character plus 1 per character, then <strong>+10% per fragment already cleared in the current combo</strong>. <code>("wait,")</code> has five punctuation characters and nine characters, so it opens a combo at 59.</li>
      <li><strong>The cost of a leak:</strong> a fragment that reaches the gutter costs <strong>one shield</strong> and <strong>resets your combo to zero</strong>. It does not cost points. Three leaks and the round is over.</li>
      <li>There is no penalty for typing the wrong thing. If nothing on screen starts with what you have typed the field turns red — press <kbd>Enter</kbd> or <kbd>Esc</kbd> to empty it and start again.</li>
      <li><strong>The storm builds.</strong> Spawn interval falls from 1.60s toward 0.42s and fragments fall faster, purely as a function of how long you have been playing. Playing well does not make it worse; surviving does.</li>
      <li>The <a href="/settings/">Skip punctuation</a> setting is deliberately ignored here — honouring it would delete the game. It still applies on the practice surface.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
